  "verificationScope": "For a commutative ring R,a finite family of arbitrary R-modules P_i,the canonical assembly of component functionals is a linear equivalence from the product of component duals to the dual of the product. Its restriction to the original Pi.single coordinate is the original component functional,and its evaluation is the finite sum of original component pairings. Uses mathlib's original DFinsupp universal linear equivalence and finite function equivalence. No dimension hypothesis or independently supplied dual comparison. The actual original tuple dual map is proved to have the transposes of the original proj_j T single_i entries. The ACTUAL categorical ModuleCat biproduct coordinates preserve original inclusions and projections. For an ARBITRARY actual categorical map u between finite biproducts,the matrix of the duals of its actual original categorical entries is proved to commute with its original tuple dual under canonical dual assembly. In addition,the original homogeneous coefficient map of any actual coefficient ring equivalence is proved invertible and compatible with original homogeneous multiplication. It is specialized to the ACTUAL canonical Scheme.GammaSpecIso K<->Gamma(Spec K,O):no coefficient ring equivalence is an input to that specialization. Its forward coefficient map is proved identical to the original coefficient map used in the published native top-Cech matrix,and its inverse is the original reverse affine comparison. The four named local inverse-pair instances are STRUCTURAL DEFINITIONS derived from existing proved RingEquiv inverse data,not assumptions. This twenty-seven-declaration continuation is OUTSIDE immutable36. Geometric native Cech/algebraic Hom dual alignment,base-ring coefficient comparison,arbitrary integer regrading,Koszul restriction,fixed-m sections,canonical dualizing identification and original4.1/4.2/main remain OPEN or UNVERIFIED.",
  "remainingObligations": [
    "Specialize the proved actual finite-biproduct/dual coordinate matrix square to original graded coefficient pieces and relation entries",
    "Extend the proved actual canonical homogeneous coefficient equivalences to dual functionals and original graded matrix entries;assemble the whole K versus Gamma(Spec K,O) dual/cokernel square",
    "Arbitrary original integer-twist regrading,Koszul compatibility,fixed-m sections and dualizing identification remain OPEN",
    "Original4.1,original4.2 and main remain OPEN;no whole-project checkpoint promoted"
  ],
